//! Ruskel generates skeletonized versions of Rust crates.
//!
//! It produces a single-page, syntactically valid Rust code representation of a
//! crate, with all implementations omitted. This provides a clear overview of
//! the crate's structure and public API.
//!
//! Ruskel works by first fetching all dependencies, then using the nightly Rust
//! toolchain to generate JSON documentation data. This data is then parsed and
//! rendered into the skeletonized format. The skeletonized code is then
//! formatted with rustfmt, and optionally has syntax highlighting applied.
//!
//!
//! You must have the nightly Rust toolchain installed to use (but not to
//! install) Ruskel.
//!
//! Canonical workspace snapshots are captured separately through
//! [`Ruskel::capture_snapshot`]. Capture returns an in-memory [`ApiSnapshot`]
//! and never writes a destination directory.

